  "title": "# Data set bar plugin (Brett) A plugin that attaches to ANY data set (grid, list, tree, table) and …",
  "asked": "# Data set bar plugin (Brett) A plugin that attaches to ANY data set (grid, list, tree, table) and is hidden by default. - Search, Filter and Sort are each their own registry asset (search-bar, filter-button, sort-control), reusable on their own, plus a combined 'data set bar' asset. - Attach: right-click any data set -> 'Attach data set bar' (or attach pieces individually), with placement top/bottom/inline/floating. Detach the same way. Also attachable from the Registry Browser, by voice, and via API/MCP/CLI. - Filter: per-column/field rules, saved filters. Sort: multi-key, saved. Search: field-scoped, fuzzy. - Per-attachment config stored locally (local-first), with Reset to default. - Existing top-bar search widget becomes an instance of the search-bar asset. - Submit at least 3 UI options to UI Review first. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
